    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside tandem in the outfield, with **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.48) representing our clearest paths to production. **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Peralta, benefiting from a 10% park boost and an advantageous batting order slot, while **Corbin Carroll** remains our elite weapon for stolen base accumulation; his matchup against Hughes is bolstered by a strong platoon profile and an Order #2 designation. Further down the order, **Mickey Moniak** (61.43) is a surprisingly strong play today, largely due to a massive 14% dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed Soroka, ensuring he provides significant value despite a middle-of-the-pack spot in the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today centered on **Gabriel Moreno** (57.18) and **Brice Turang** (58.71), both of whom flirted with the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold. While **Brice Turang** provides the stolen base floor we covet, his score was slightly hampered by the skill of Mize on the mound. Conversely, **Gabriel Moreno** offers consistent contact and a solid Order #3 placement, though he sits just below our ideal start tier. With **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Jose Caballero** all unavailable due to IL stints or off-days, our bench depth is heavily compromised, leaving players like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** to monitor for potential mid-week rotations. \n\nThe primary risk today is the reliance on the middle-to-bottom of the order. **Austin Riley** (50.50) is teetering on a marginal status; while his raw talent is undeniable, he faces a tough assignment against Scott and is pushed down to the #7 spot, limiting his RBI opportunities. We are effectively betting on our top-order spark plugs\u2014**Corbin Carroll** and **Tyler Soderstrom**\u2014to mitigate the volatility presented by **Henry Bolte** and **Austin Riley**. As we push for the stretch run, maintaining these game caps while chasing the scarce SB category remains the priority, even if the projections for our bottom-half hitters remain conservative.",
